#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""usd-repl: an OpenUSD C++ REPL on top of clang-repl.

    repl/usd-repl                                     an empty session
    repl/usd-repl nvidia_tutorials/08_xform/main.cpp  run a lesson, keep the prompt
    repl/usd-repl --batch FILE...                     run files, exit 1 on any error
    repl/usd-repl --emit FILE...                      print the inputs a file becomes

clang-repl 18 runs the code; this script sits in front of it. It reads whole
blocks (brackets balanced, statements finished) and rewrites the shapes
clang-repl 18 gets wrong: top-level loops, ifs and try blocks run inside a
lambda. It prints bare expressions through repl/usd_repl.h. It keeps a journal
of the inputs that worked, so a crash, Ctrl-C or %undo rebuilds the session in
a fresh clang-repl. With prompt_toolkit installed, input is edited and
highlighted as in IPython; with Pygments, output is coloured. The README's REPL
section has the details and the reasons.
"""

